1. What you may do

1.1 You may read, copy and change the Software.

1.2 You may run the Software, with or without changes, for development and
    testing. This needs no plan.

1.3 You may use the Software in production only for a company that has a valid
    OpenAct Director or OpenAct Producer plan. A company has a valid plan when
    one of these is true:
    a. The company has a paid subscription to the plan from MarketGrowth, and
       the subscription is active.
    b. The OpenAct deploy has a license key that MarketGrowth issued, and the
       key is valid for that plan, that deploy and that date.

1.4 You may keep the Software in an OpenAct deploy where companies without a
    valid plan cannot use it. The Software locks itself for those companies.
    Keeping it locked is not production use.

1.5 You may send changes to MarketGrowth, for example as a pull request.


2. What you must not do

2.1 You must not remove, change, disable or work around the plan check, the
    license key check or the billing code to use the Software without a valid
    plan. This includes, but is not limited to:
    a. changing the "plan" field in this folder's package.json;
    b. adding public keys to, or changing, license-keys.ts in the core;
    c. setting up your own billing account to sell plans to yourself or to others;
    d. changing the core so that a locked app does not lock.

2.2 You must not sell, rent, sublicense or give the Software, or changes to it,
    to other people, except as a full copy of the OpenAct repository that
    includes this file.

2.3 You must not offer the Software to other people as a hosted service, unless
    MarketGrowth agrees in writing.

2.4 You must not remove or change copyright, license or other notices in the
    Software.


3. Contributions

If you send a change to MarketGrowth, you give MarketGrowth the right to use,
